senses.gloss:
Krimila,
(1) n. of a mountain: Māy 〔253.32〕;
(2) n. of a maharṣi: Māy 〔257.5〕.

krīḍāpanaka,
(1) nt. (= Pali kīḷāpanaka. Skt. only krīḍanaka), toy, plaything: Kashgar rec. and 1 Nep. ms. at SP 〔74.1〕 (prose; ed. krīḍanaka); Mv 〔ii.434.1—4〕; 〔475.7〕;
(2) m., of animals and men, plaything, animal or person to be used for amusement: SP 〔94.6〕 (vs) sudurbalāḥ śvānaśṛgālabhūtāḥ [] pareṣa (or ˚ṣu) krīḍāpanakā bhavanti; Mv 〔ii.479.16〕 antaḥpurikānāṃ krīḍāpanako bhavatu (subject, Kuśa disguised as a cook), 18; 〔488.21〕; 〔iii.16.3〕 antaḥpuraṃ praveśīyati krīḍāpanako bhaviṣyati;
(3) fem. ˚panikā, foll. by dhātrī, = krīḍanikā, q.v.; Divy 〔475.13, 17〕. (Cf. AMg. kīlāvaṇa-dhāī, beside kīlaṇa-dhāī.)
